  "change": "G3 reads authoritative Card dependencies through a public typed port, emits prerequisite-to-dependent precedes owned by the dependent Card, serializes cycle checks with the Board fence, and publishes durable mutation events including removed row identity. Consumers are selected by direct relational dependency within the Board. Native active sets preserve foreign provenance and compensate failures.",
  "coverage": "The real service admits all nine normal/test/bug pairs; the planner preserves their physical types, direction and persisted dependency identity. Native tests cover the four Entity/Bug layouts, removal, pending endpoints, parallel human and unrelated provenance, repeated compensation and post-delete failure. The ordinary queue materializes typed dependencies, replays without duplicates and converges removals. Real SQL transactions exercise writer interleaving and cycle refusal; an application use case rejects cross-Board links even for an owner of both Boards. Durable outbox retains add/remove and avoids duplicate events.",
